# Netlify fallback rules.
#
# The build prerenders every indexable route to its own HTML file, so there is
# deliberately no `/*  /index.html  200` catch-all here any more. That rule
# used to answer every dead URL with the homepage at HTTP 200, which Search
# Console records as a soft 404 against the homepage.
#
# Netlify serves 404.html with a real 404 status for unmatched paths on its
# own, so unknown URLs now behave correctly with no rule at all.
#
# Legacy paths from the previous site, kept as permanent redirects so any
# existing inbound links and their accumulated authority carry over.
/policies      /info/policies     301
/competitive   /competition-team  301
/locations     /dance-classes     301
